'''Orrimaarko'''<ref name="Card Trader">{{SWCT|set=Topps Choice 2|cardname=Orrimaarko}}</ref> was a [[Gender|male]]<ref name="Resistance Reborn" /> [[Dressellian]]<ref name="Alien Archive" /> who served the [[Alliance to Restore the Republic]] during the [[Galactic Civil War]] against the [[Galactic Empire]]. Shortly before the [[Battle of Endor]], in which the Alliance attacked the Empire's [[DS-2 Death Star II Mobile Battle Station]] [[superweapon]] above the [[moon]] of [[Endor]],<ref name="ROTJ" /> he<ref name="Resistance Reborn" /> attended a meeting on board the [[MC80 Star Cruiser]] ''[[Home One]]'' to plan the battle. Orrimaarko would go on to serve on the [[Endor strike team]] under [[General]] [[Han Solo]], travelling to the [[Endor|Forest Moon of Endor]] aboard the captured [[Lambda-class T-4a shuttle|''Lambda''-class T-4a shuttle]] ''Tydirium''.<ref name="ROTJ" />

He had light [[Color|brown]] skin and black [[eye]]s, although one was covered by an eye patch.<ref name="ROTJ" />

==Behind the scenes==
Orrimaarko first appeared in [[Star Wars: Episode VI Return of the Jedi|''Star Wars'': Episode VI ''Return of the Jedi'']].<ref name="ROTJ" /> His 1984 action figure was labeled "Prune Face,"<ref name="Databank">{{DB|character|orrimaarko|Orrimaarko}}</ref> the only name the character had until [[Pablo Hidalgo]] dubbed him Orrimaarko in ''[[Galaxy Guide 12: Aliens — Enemies and Allies]]'' a [[Star Wars Legends|''Star Wars'' Legends]] sourcebook by [[West End Games]] released in [[1995]].<ref name="gg12">''[[Galaxy Guide 12: Aliens — Enemies and Allies]]''</ref>

The [[2018]] reference book ''[[Star Wars: Alien Archive]]'' states that Orrimaarko was a member of the Endor strike team during the Battle of Endor.<ref name="Alien Archive" />, a fact confirmed when he is seen aboard the ''Tydirium'' standing behind Han Solo as he entered the cockpit of the shuttle.<ref name="ROTJ" /> However, in the [[2019]] novel ''[[Resistance Reborn]]'', however, in conversation with [[Leia Skywalker Organa Solo|Leia Organa]] Orrimaarko specifically states that he did not fight on the ground during the battle.<ref name="Resistance Reborn" />

